<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Shimazu clan domain</h1><p class="st-meta">1550 CE – 1600 CE (approx.) · capital Kagoshima</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The domain of the Shimazu of southern Kyushu, who nearly conquered the whole island before submitting to Toyotomi Hideyoshi in 1587.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-clan">Shimazu</a> had been governors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> period but had splintered into rival branches. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-takahisa">Shimazu Takahisa</a> reunited the clan and province by about 1550, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagoshima">Kagoshima</a>. Portuguese guns reached the Shimazu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanegashima">Tanegashima</a> in 1543, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-xavier">Francis Xavier</a> landed at Kagoshima in 1549.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-takahisa">Takahisa</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-yoshihisa">Yoshihisa</a> and his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-yoshihiro">Yoshihiro</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-toshihisa">Toshihisa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-iehisa">Iehisa</a> formed a formidable military team. They conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osumi-province">Osumi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyuga-province">Hyuga</a>, crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otomo-clan">Otomo</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mimikawa">Mimikawa</a> in 1578 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryuzoji-clan">Ryuzoji</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okitanawate">Okitanawate</a> in 1584, and by 1586 controlled most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>. The domain drew strength from a large warrior class and trade through its ports.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> in 1587 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-yoshihisa">Yoshihisa</a> surrendered, keeping <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osumi-province">Osumi</a>. After fighting for the losing side at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-clan">Shimazu</a> negotiated to keep their lands as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/satsuma-domain">Satsuma Domain</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/shimazu-clan-domain.jpg" alt="Shimazu clan domain" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Sarang · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maru_ni_J%C5%AB-monji_(Kutsuwa)_inverted.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1550 CE – 1600 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kagoshima</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shimazu Takahisa, Shimazu Yoshihisa, Shimazu Yoshihiro</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Japanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Shimazu clan, Shimazu of Satsuma</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1575&amp;focus=shimazu-clan-domain" aria-label="Shimazu clan domain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8047 1027 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Shimazu clan domain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8367 1283L8440 1178M8367 1283L8367 1283"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M844